---
source: crates/trust-cg-test/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_of(&[\"report\"])"
---
Generate the weekly Trust Codegen dashboard (WS9).

Reads the newest compatible JSON recursively from each known workstream result directory, renders
the north-star table and per-workstream sections, and marks missing data with `—`. Writes
`reports/weekly/<iso-date>.md` by default.

# Examples

  trust-cg-test report
  trust-cg-test report --week 2026-04-19 --format human
  trust-cg-test report --out /tmp/weekly.md

Usage: trust-cg-test report [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (human, json, junit)

          Possible values:
          - human: Pretty table + narrative, targeted at humans
          - json:  Machine-readable JSON
          - junit: JUnit XML for CI consumers

          [default: human]

      --week <ISO-DATE>
          ISO date for the report. Default: today (UTC)

      --markdown-out <PATH>
          Markdown target path (takes precedence over `--out`)

  -o, --out <PATH>
          Override the command-specific output file or directory.

          See the selected subcommand's help for its output type and default.

      --publish
          Also copy the report to `reports/weekly/` and write `reports/dashboard.md`, even when a
          custom output path is selected

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-unit timeout in seconds. Subcommands may apply per-unit defaults when this is unset

      --parallel <N>
          Worker count (honors cargo-serialization lock). Default: auto

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress bars; errors still go to stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          Show debug-level events. Repeat for more: -vv, -vvv

      --no-cache
          Ignore proof / corpus caches

      --dry-run
          Print what would run without executing external tools

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
